# Death by old age erases the save, and Continue goes with it.
#
# One of three death scripts (see death_starvation.cli, death_wounds.cli). Each proves the same two
# things for a different cause: the death screen names it, and the run cannot be continued afterwards.
# That second half is what makes the save system ironman rather than merely automatic — the save is
# deleted in TriggerDeath, the funnel for all three causes, so it goes even if the player force-quits
# at the death screen instead of pressing END RUN.
#
# Reached with --advance-days, which is applied on the first arrival at the world map immediately
# BEFORE the old-age check — so a shove past any possible lifetime (the heart tops out at 43,200 days)
# kills on arrival with no journey needed.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --advance-days 45000 --save-path .tmp-cli-save/death-age.json

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue

# The clock is shoved past the lifetime before the world map becomes interactive, so the run ends
# without the player ever choosing a destination.
wait mode Death 45
expect OLD AGE
expect END RUN

# Permadeath: the save is gone the moment the death fires, before END RUN is pressed.
expect-state savefile save none

click end-run
wait mode MainMenu 20

# Nothing to continue, and the menu says so.
# Continue is state, not pixels — a disabled button differs only by colour on screen, so
# this is asserted through inspect rather than by scanning the terminal.
inspect menu
expect-state menu Continue disabled

quit
